Paths below describe the Git source tree; installation ZIPs carry only the
selected runtime files and generated configs. Full source and provenance:
https://github.com/rpcyan586/svzero-profiles

Public upstream inputs:
- source/vendor-profiles: selected unmodified profile JSONs from
  Sovol3d/Sovol-OrcaSlicer, with a pinned commit and SHA-256 inventory in
  source/vendor-profiles/provenance.json. The upstream repository carries
  AGPL-3.0 in OrcaSlicer/LICENSE.txt; a copy is in LICENSES/AGPL-3.0.txt.
  Generation modifies the machine root to describe a single-material printer.
- source/vendor-profiles/OrcaSlicer: six unmodified Sovol Zero filament JSONs
  from OrcaSlicer/OrcaSlicer, added there by Eric McCann in PR #15756, with a
  pinned commit and SHA-256 inventory in its own provenance.json. OrcaSlicer is
  AGPL-3.0 (LICENSE.txt); a copy is in LICENSES/AGPL-3.0.txt. Generation reads
  their nozzle temperatures and flow caps through
  source/filament-nozzle-upstream.json.
- source/ps3: PrusaSlicer schema files, AGPL-3.0. Their provenance is recorded
  alongside them; the full licence is in LICENSES/AGPL-3.0.txt.
- Source tables retain stock numerical reference settings used for comparisons.
  They are development inputs, not selectable Stock presets.

Sovol-derived Klipper macros:
klipper/config/cancel_print.cfg, end_print.cfg, filament_load.cfg,
nozzle_brush.cfg and start_print.cfg carry text from Sovol's Macro.cfg. The
Zero's copy (https://github.com/Sovol3d/SOVOL-ZERO) has no licence file, but
Sovol publishes the same macros under GPL-3.0 in
https://github.com/Sovol3d/SV08 -- commit a60644875f8c,
home/sovol/printer_data/config/Macro.cfg, blob e584b9d1c2a2 -- and that text
is used here under that licence. Compared line by line (2026-10-13):
LOAD_FILAMENT and UNLOAD_FILAMENT are identical in both, and every Sovol line
in filament_load.cfg and nozzle_brush.cfg is in the SV08 file. The few lines
with no GPL-3.0 source are calls to Sovol macros by name (ALL_FAN_OFF,
CHANG_ROOT_MAIN, save_last_file), standard Klipper commands, the Zero's pin
assignments and park position, and three M117 status messages. Sovol states
that the Zero is "fully open-source (including hardware, firmware, and
structure)" under "the open-source guidelines of Voron and Klipper" (SOVOL-ZERO
README).

The bed texture PNG is "Sovol Zero buildplate texture" by Chinchill
(https://www.printables.com/model/1263730), unmodified, under Creative Commons
Attribution 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/); its copy with a
10 mm grid added, for PrusaSlicer and SuperSlicer, is under the same licence. The bed SVG is
an original schematic preview, GPL-3.0. The bed STL is Sovol's
own CAD for the Zero's hotbed (STEP/hotbed kit.STEP in
https://github.com/Sovol3d/SOVOL-ZERO, which has no licence file; see Sovol's
statement above), tessellated, placed in the slicer frame and simplified. The
two lead screws added to it, raised by the 152.4 mm print height, are GPL-3.0.
Credits: assets/svzero_bed.CREDITS.md. Neither is derived from the third-party
assets used in earlier private builds.
The original artwork and the optional Orca validator binary are not distributed.
